1
00:00:00,080 --> 00:00:02,002
Millions of people own stocks.

2
00:00:02,052 --> 00:00:04,349
On Robinhood Chain, stocks are tokens,

3
00:00:04,399 --> 00:00:06,613
but a token earns nothing while it sits.

4
00:00:06,663 --> 00:00:09,205
Wall Street holders sell
covered calls for income,

5
00:00:09,255 --> 00:00:11,509
but someone must pick each week's strike,

6
00:00:11,559 --> 00:00:12,716
and you must trust them.

7
00:00:12,766 --> 00:00:13,884
On-chain it's harder:

8
00:00:13,934 --> 00:00:15,969
multipliers easy to apply twice,

9
00:00:16,019 --> 00:00:17,329
weekend price freezes,

10
00:00:17,379 --> 00:00:18,908
pauses, mid-week splits.

11
00:00:18,958 --> 00:00:20,450
So tokens sit idle,

12
00:00:20,500 --> 00:00:22,553
or go to managers nobody can check.

13
00:00:22,603 --> 00:00:25,662
Now imagine an agent picking
the strike each week,

14
00:00:25,712 --> 00:00:27,535
held to the rules by a contract.

15
00:00:27,585 --> 00:00:28,447
This is Strike:

16
00:00:28,497 --> 00:00:30,457
options vaults for stock tokens.

17
00:00:30,507 --> 00:00:32,582
Weekly premium in USDG.

18
00:00:32,632 --> 00:00:35,669
An AI agent picks the
strike, inside a mandate.

19
00:00:35,719 --> 00:00:38,441
Break it, and its bond goes to depositors.

20
00:00:38,491 --> 00:00:40,413
Rust on Stylus does the math.

21
00:00:40,463 --> 00:00:43,678
Live on Robinhood Chain
and Arbitrum Sepolia.

22
00:00:43,728 --> 00:00:44,879
Inside one week:

23
00:00:44,929 --> 00:00:47,414
Depositors fill a vault
with a fixed mandate.

24
00:00:47,464 --> 00:00:50,425
An agent reads it via MCP and dry-runs.

25
00:00:50,475 --> 00:00:53,464
It proposes delta, expiry, size and price.

26
00:00:53,514 --> 00:00:57,065
The Epoch Manager checks the
mandate at guarded oracle prices.

27
00:00:57,115 --> 00:00:59,722
Rust on Stylus solves and
stress-tests the strike.

28
00:00:59,772 --> 00:01:02,933
If it passes, buyers pay premium in USDG.

29
00:01:02,983 --> 00:01:05,515
If not, the bond is slashed to depositors.

30
00:01:05,565 --> 00:01:07,355
Decisions are hashed on-chain;

31
00:01:07,405 --> 00:01:10,583
the agent has an ERC-8004 identity.

32
00:01:10,633 --> 00:01:11,948
Friday's close settles;

33
00:01:11,998 --> 00:01:14,527
depositors get the premium, less a fee.

34
00:01:14,577 --> 00:01:18,211
Same contracts on Robinhood
Chain and Arbitrum Sepolia.

35
00:01:18,261 --> 00:01:20,183
Say Maya opens the Tesla vault.

36
00:01:20,233 --> 00:01:24,855
This week it sold the $369.86 call:

37
00:01:24,905 --> 00:01:27,155
four options, 10.01 USDG.

38
00:01:27,205 --> 00:01:29,614
At or below the strike, Maya keeps it;

39
00:01:29,664 --> 00:01:33,314
the buyer profits above $372.36.

40
00:01:33,364 --> 00:01:35,005
The limits are in the contract:

41
00:01:35,055 --> 00:01:38,104
Delta 0.10 to 0.35,

42
00:01:38,154 --> 00:01:40,648
at least 95% of fair value,

43
00:01:40,697 --> 00:01:43,444
at least 0.05% yield,

44
00:01:43,494 --> 00:01:45,081
at most 80% sold,

45
00:01:45,131 --> 00:01:46,141
1 to 8 days,

46
00:01:46,191 --> 00:01:47,270
fixed for good.

47
00:01:47,320 --> 00:01:49,462
The playground tests proposals live,

48
00:01:49,512 --> 00:01:50,214
no wallet.

49
00:01:50,264 --> 00:01:53,301
An honest 0.20-delta call: accepted.

50
00:01:53,351 --> 00:01:55,194
A reckless at-the-money strike:

51
00:01:55,244 --> 00:01:57,169
rejected, delta out of band.

52
00:01:57,219 --> 00:02:01,767
A real one costs the agent
10 USDG, paid to depositors.

53
00:02:01,817 --> 00:02:03,805
Buyers pay at the moment they buy:

54
00:02:03,855 --> 00:02:06,925
oracle spot moved 0.5% against them,

55
00:02:06,974 --> 00:02:09,482
Black-Scholes, times the agent's factor.

56
00:02:09,532 --> 00:02:11,205
Never below intrinsic value,

57
00:02:11,255 --> 00:02:13,690
so stale prices can't be picked off.

58
00:02:13,740 --> 00:02:16,234
The vault ran live on September 29.

59
00:02:16,284 --> 00:02:19,231
The seller agent asked for 0.20 delta;

60
00:02:19,281 --> 00:02:23,616
the contract solved $369.86, accepted.

61
00:02:23,666 --> 00:02:26,217
A reckless agent forced
an at-the-money put:

62
00:02:26,267 --> 00:02:28,525
rejected, 10 USDG slashed,

63
00:02:28,575 --> 00:02:30,319
bond 60 to 50.

64
00:02:30,369 --> 00:02:34,073
The explorer says Success:
a rejection isn't a revert,

65
00:02:34,123 --> 00:02:36,421
and 10 USDG left the bond.

66
00:02:36,471 --> 00:02:39,413
On Arbitrum Sepolia, Claude
planned the proposal.

67
00:02:39,463 --> 00:02:42,240
Via Claude Code and Strike's MCP server,

68
00:02:42,290 --> 00:02:43,148
it read the vault

69
00:02:43,198 --> 00:02:45,024
and dry-ran five candidates.

70
00:02:45,074 --> 00:02:49,168
It chose 0.20 delta at 105% of fair value,

71
00:02:49,218 --> 00:02:50,320
and wrote why:

72
00:02:50,370 --> 00:02:52,530
mid-band, safe from small moves.

73
00:02:52,580 --> 00:02:56,632
The contract solved $364.29: accepted.

74
00:02:56,682 --> 00:02:57,506
On Arbiscan:

75
00:02:57,556 --> 00:02:59,757
a successful call from the agent's signer.

76
00:02:59,807 --> 00:03:02,728
The same run slashed a
reckless put 10 USDG,

77
00:03:02,778 --> 00:03:04,679
and a buyer took all 4 calls.

78
00:03:04,729 --> 00:03:05,614
In 3D:

79
00:03:05,664 --> 00:03:09,022
Across, Tesla's price. Back, days left.

80
00:03:09,072 --> 00:03:10,653
Up, a share's value.

81
00:03:10,703 --> 00:03:15,063
At expiry it bends flat
at the $364.29 strike:

82
00:03:15,113 --> 00:03:16,702
upside goes to the buyer.

83
00:03:16,752 --> 00:03:21,119
Below, the depositor keeps
stock plus $2.23 per option.

84
00:03:21,169 --> 00:03:23,597
The math is Rust, on Arbitrum Stylus.

85
00:03:23,647 --> 00:03:26,413
Solving a strike takes
48 Black-Scholes runs:

86
00:03:26,463 --> 00:03:29,079
6.5 times less gas than Solidity,

87
00:03:29,129 --> 00:03:31,671
3.3 times less per proposal.

88
00:03:31,721 --> 00:03:33,569
Every run leaves a decision record.

89
00:03:33,619 --> 00:03:35,931
Its hash is anchored in the DecisionLog;

90
00:03:35,981 --> 00:03:38,577
rehash the file, and it matches the chain.

91
00:03:38,627 --> 00:03:40,918
Its ERC-8004 identity:

92
00:03:40,968 --> 00:03:46,235
114 on Robinhood Chain testnet,
253 on Arbitrum Sepolia.

93
00:03:46,285 --> 00:03:48,394
Anyone can join, no allow-list.

94
00:03:48,444 --> 00:03:49,114
The monitor,

95
00:03:49,164 --> 00:03:50,366
live on mainnet:

96
00:03:50,416 --> 00:03:55,569
Nvidia's multiplier, 1.000775,
is already in the price,

97
00:03:55,619 --> 00:03:57,764
so Strike never applies it twice.

98
00:03:57,814 --> 00:04:00,585
Over 403 weeks since 2019,

99
00:04:00,635 --> 00:04:04,308
covered calls cut volatility 25 to 46%,

100
00:04:04,358 --> 00:04:06,110
but lagged holding everywhere:

101
00:04:06,160 --> 00:04:10,862
Tesla 23.1% a year, against 44.0% held.

102
00:04:10,912 --> 00:04:13,031
And it assumes full weekly sales.

103
00:04:13,081 --> 00:04:14,032
The proof page:

104
00:04:14,082 --> 00:04:16,251
891 tests and proofs,

105
00:04:16,301 --> 00:04:18,618
99.3% line coverage,

106
00:04:18,669 --> 00:04:20,038
nine Halmos proofs,

107
00:04:20,088 --> 00:04:22,125
all 11 review findings fixed.

108
00:04:22,175 --> 00:04:23,288
Who else is here?

109
00:04:23,338 --> 00:04:26,941
Stonkhouse and Archer Markets on
Robinhood Chain are order books:

110
00:04:26,992 --> 00:04:28,860
traders pick strike and price.

111
00:04:28,910 --> 00:04:32,566
Ribbon, Derive and Thetanuts
sell crypto options

112
00:04:32,617 --> 00:04:34,499
by auction, order book or RFQ.

113
00:04:34,549 --> 00:04:37,443
Tilt's AI manages vaults, with no options;

114
00:04:37,493 --> 00:04:40,964
its sources don't say
what limits it on-chain.

115
00:04:41,014 --> 00:04:43,385
In Strike, a bonded agent proposes,

116
00:04:43,435 --> 00:04:45,780
the contract enforces mandate and price,

117
00:04:45,830 --> 00:04:47,070
and rule-breakers pay.

118
00:04:47,120 --> 00:04:49,566
Stock-token traps are handled on-chain.

119
00:04:49,616 --> 00:04:51,935
Holders get income and keep their keys.

120
00:04:51,985 --> 00:04:55,479
Weekend freezes: settle on
the first post-expiry price.

121
00:04:55,529 --> 00:04:58,223
Multiplier: never applied, fork-tested.

122
00:04:58,273 --> 00:05:01,415
Agent trust: fixed
mandate, bond, slashing.

123
00:05:01,465 --> 00:05:04,740
Gas: Rust on Stylus, 6.5 times cheaper.

124
00:05:04,790 --> 00:05:07,519
Not done: no audit, and testnet only.

125
00:05:07,569 --> 00:05:10,420
Strike: options on Robinhood
Chain and Arbitrum,

126
00:05:10,470 --> 00:05:12,884
run by agents held to a mandate.
